# VCU Triangulation Gate

Before any VCU lesson, skill, or project task is accepted:

- Round 1 requires at least two independent reviews against the same source manifest.
- Revision must address every disagreement, blocked claim, or low-confidence finding.
- Round 2 reviews only the delta and must not introduce new unreviewed scope.
- Publish requires real install logs, real test logs, link verification, RLS/access review, and an explicit no-mock pass.

If any evidence is missing, keep the lesson or task `review`, `blocked`, or `unverified`; never mark it `published` or `completed`.
